WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.320
A lot of the work people want automated lives on their computer.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.449
Behind a sign-in. In an app with no API. In an Excel file.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.036
Now those jobs are yours.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.367
Describe the job,

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.970
and Kitewell lays out every step for you to check.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.515
Prefer code? It's plain YAML.

00:00:24.515 --> 00:00:28.116
Build it from Claude Code or Codex, over MCP.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.272
It runs on their computer, and their passwords stay there.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.855
It does the clicking: websites, desktop apps, and email.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.224
It stops for their OK where it matters,

00:00:40.224 --> 00:00:42.473
and keeps a record of every step.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.007
Got a list in Excel?

00:00:47.007 --> 00:00:50.871
It runs for every row, and writes each result back beside it.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.803
It learns the clicks once, replays them without the model,

00:00:54.803 --> 00:00:57.231
and relearns when a page changes.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.661
If a run fails, the alert names the step, in your Slack.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.942
Fix it on your laptop, and the fix reaches their computer.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.800
What you teach goes into the project's notes,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.377
for whoever takes over.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.018
You build it. Their computers do the work.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.260
Kitewell.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.010
It flies on its own.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.306
You hold the string.
